0. So total is 1260. Wait, 72*1260=72*(1200+60)=86400+4320=90720. Yes, so total permutations are 1260.\n\nNow, compute |A|: number of permutations where all three a's are adjacent. Treat the three a's as a single entity. So, we have this \"AAA\" block, plus the four b's, two c's. So, total entities: 1 + 4 + 2 = 7 entities. But wait, the four b's are identical and the two c's are identical. So, the number of permutations is 7! / (1!4!2!) = 7! / (4!2!) = 5040 / (24*2) = 5040 / 48 = 105. So, |A| = 105.\n\nSimilarly, |B|: all four b's are adjacent. Treat \"BBBB\" as a single entity. Then we have three a's, one \"BBBB\", two c's. Total entities: 3 + 1 + 2 = 6. Number of permutations: 6! / (3!1!2!) = 720 / (6*1*2) = 720 / 12 = 60. So, |B| = 60.\n\n|C|: both c's are adjacent. Treat \"CC\" as a single entity. Then we have three a's, four b's, one \"CC\". Total entities: 3 + 4 + 1 = 8. Number of permutations: 8! / (3!4!1!) = 40320 / (6*24*1) = 40320 / 144 = 280. So, |C| = 280.\n\nNow, compute the intersections. |A\u2229B|: both all a's and all b's are adjacent. So, treat \"AAA\" and \"BBBB\" as single entities. Then we have \"AAA\", \"BBBB\", two c's. Total entities: 1 + 1 + 2 = 4. Number of permutations: 4! / (1!1!2!) = 24 / (1*1*2) = 12. Wait, but in this case, the letters are \"AAA\", \"BBBB\", \"C\", \"C\". Wait, but \"C\"s are two separate, but treated as a single entity? Wait, no. Wait, when we treat \"AAA\" and \"BBBB\" as single entities, the remaining letters are two c's. So, the total number of entities is 1 (AAA) + 1 (BBBB) + 2 (C's) = 4? Wait, no. Wait, each c is separate? Wait, no. Wait, if we are treating \"AAA\" and \"BBBB\" as blocks, then the two c's are still separate letters. Wait, no. Wait, the original letters are three a's, four b's, two c's. If we group all a's into a single block and all b's into a single block, then we have three entities: \"AAA\", \"BBBB\", and the two c's. Wait, but the two c's are two separate letters. So, actually, the total numb